Description: Xpra client written in Rust
 An Xpra client implemented in Rust, built on winit and softbuffer - no GTK
 or Qt dependency. It speaks the Xpra protocol over tcp, ssl, ws, wss and
 ssh, and decodes the jpeg, png and webp picture encodings.
 .
 This is a proof of concept and requires an xpra 6.6 or later server.
 .
 The binary is installed as `rust-xpra` so that it does not collide with the
 `xpra` package, which owns /usr/bin/xpra.
